# Skill origin

Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.

New Cursor artifacts go in one of these three trees under `.cursor/skills|hooks|rules/`:

| Tree | Put it here when |
|---|---|
| `autodevelop/` | Autodevelop product or workflow, including generic rules we authored (process, cybersecurity, frontend, design, testing, documents). |
| `<client-name>/` | Their board, domains, people, shipping process, or other client IP. Only in the client repo (or optional fork). |
| `third-party/` | Vendored from open source. Do not edit except to vendor-update. |

Same split for skills, hooks, and rules. Do not reuse a skill folder name or rule filename across trees.

- Do **not** add a fourth top-level category folder (no `.cursor/rules/frontend/` beside `autodevelop/`). Fold authored rules under `autodevelop/<category>/`.
- Do not put client or product names in `autodevelop/` or `third-party/`.
- Do not open-source the consumer instance folder.
- Product app code (CORS, `package.json`, GHA) stays in the app, not under `.cursor/skills`.
- Rules, skills, and hooks **created in chat** that belong to the Autodevelop workflow go under `.cursor/{rules,skills,hooks}/autodevelop/…`.
- New Devrecated `SKILL.md` and `.mdc` files include `Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.`
- Every file that ships to a customer (`kits/`, plugin payload, customer CLI) includes `Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.` JSON that a host schema owns gets a `copyright` field; markdown and scripts get the usual header.

Instance bindings (board ids, preview project, mail allowlist, `.policies/`, `.configuration/`) live in the consumer `.autodevelop/` folder (legacy: `<client-name>/autodevelop/`). The starter copy is `kits/autodevelop/`. Do not put live ids in the user-scope plugin.

This repository keeps a dogfood workspace and two shippable kits:

| Tree | Role |
|---|---|
| `.cursor/` | What this Autodevelop checkout uses to operate on itself. Cursor loads it as the workspace kit. |
| `kits/cursor/` | The shippable Cursor shim. `plugin.json` and `pnpm autodevelop:import` point here. |
| `kits/autodevelop/` | The shippable starter bind. Install copies missing files into consumer `.autodevelop/`. |
| `.autodevelop/` | Live bind for **this** checkout. Not packed. |

Product rules, hooks, commands, and agents that customers should receive go in **both** places until you change them: edit `.cursor/`, then copy the file into `kits/cursor/`. Starter config and default policies live in `kits/autodevelop/`, not this checkout’s live `.autodevelop/`. Do not put a live board id, allowlist, hostname, or `services/` in `kits/`. A later agent gets `kits/<name>/`. `.cursor-plugin/` stays at the repository root.

The kit loads via **user-scope plugin install** (`/import-autodevelop` or `pnpm autodevelop:import`). The consumer repo commits `.autodevelop/` plus any `<client-name>/` trees. A fork or submodule is optional (pinning or heavy customization), not the load path.

Do not add a skill unless this chat asked. See [no-unsolicited-skills.mdc](no-unsolicited-skills.mdc).

Follow [marketplace-plugin.mdc](marketplace-plugin.mdc): add only official plugin components. This product is proprietary; do not treat public Marketplace review as the distribution path unless a human relicensed the root.
